Revision history for Authen-WebAuthn
 
Unreleased
  - Decode client-supplied CBOR with CBOR::XS->new_safe, so that a tagged
    value cannot instantiate a Perl object
  - Fix PS256 signature verification (32 byte salt)
  - Support ES384, ES512 and EdDSA (Ed25519) credential keys
  - Add allowed_algs option to validate_registration
  - origin can be an arrayref of accepted origins (Frank Carnovale)
  - Add generate_registration_options and generate_assertion_options
  - Return user_verified, backup_eligible and backup_state
  - Reject a Backup State flag without Backup Eligibility
  - Reject credential IDs longer than 1023 bytes

0.005
  - Add allow_unknown_attestation_format option

0.004
  - Add allow_untrusted_attestation option

0.003 2023-11-09
  - Update Crypt::OpenSSL::X509::Extension and Net::SSLeay dependancies
  - Make sure Net::SSLeay is initialized before use

0.002 2023-11-09
  - Supported attestation types: none, packed, fido-u2f
  - Mandatory attestation trust chain validation

0.001 2022-01-21
  - initial release
  - Authentication and registration without attestation
  - ECC/RSA keys supported
